                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ba886d1d-280b-3774-8de6-1a24c6026cb8",
                        "entry_id": "2758cacf-c589-3585-8ec7-41992c42ff62",
                        "glosses": [
                            "провести зимнее время, как правило не у себя дома; прожить где-то зимой"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "091a8479-4e59-4ba8-8935-ee1ea64f2cf3",
                                "sense_id": "ba886d1d-280b-3774-8de6-1a24c6026cb8",
                                "text": "Пришлось подумать о надежном селе, где мы могли бы перезимовать."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "352d5523-3625-4e51-93b2-3a212229e3a8",
                                "sense_id": "ba886d1d-280b-3774-8de6-1a24c6026cb8",
                                "text": "Этот матрос рассказал, что десять человек спаслись и перезимовали на каком-то острове к северу от Таймыра."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "afae5379-6de2-37b2-bb29-a521afdcb2f2",
                        "entry_id": "2758cacf-c589-3585-8ec7-41992c42ff62",
                        "glosses": [
                            "прожив зимнее время, остаться живым"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "53099294-a63a-4255-98b9-d65aa16c6a76",
                                "sense_id": "afae5379-6de2-37b2-bb29-a521afdcb2f2",
                                "text": "Из семисот с лишним человек, населявших лагерь, перезимовала только половина."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "29113b24-f555-357e-8eae-b00f11fea585",
                        "entry_id": "2758cacf-c589-3585-8ec7-41992c42ff62",
                        "glosses": [
                            "выдержать, перенести зимние холода в течение зимы (о растениях, животных)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce93295b-ea82-42f5-8e5d-f469592db227",
                                "sense_id": "29113b24-f555-357e-8eae-b00f11fea585",
                                "text": "Но пугаться этого не следует: склонившиеся привитые ветви нужно на зиму подвязать к столбикам или проволочной шпалере, и они отлично перезимуют под снегом."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f0c7bd81-fc2f-4197-9883-8f82e1733b7f",
                                "sense_id": "29113b24-f555-357e-8eae-b00f11fea585",
                                "text": "Если улей хорошо утеплён, а в сотах достаточно мёда, никакие холода пчёлам не страшны. Пчелиная семья благополучно перезимует."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c1b2e96b-ab1c-382a-bb00-0667e0530ded",
                        "entry_id": "2758cacf-c589-3585-8ec7-41992c42ff62",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., разг. пережить, перетерпеть неблагоприятное время, неприятные обстоятельства"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ce468fe5-0441-4419-91e7-1c0109b903bb",
                        "source_entry_id": "2758cacf-c589-3585-8ec7-41992c42ff62",
                        "target_lang_word": "overwinter",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "overwinter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b8456554-3b9d-32df-b589-92932c191111",
                                        "entry_id": "532925c8-2312-33b1-a0c6-790ce9ea8fa0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To keep or preserve for the winter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ecc9bfa-7406-40f4-aa8b-50c92912b2b5",
                                                "sense_id": "b8456554-3b9d-32df-b589-92932c191111",
                                                "text": "It is best to overwinter tender plants indoors."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "568db9f1-c4b7-412e-9afb-7b97b68a5a78",
                                                "sense_id": "b8456554-3b9d-32df-b589-92932c191111",
                                                "text": "Well, if you're fortunate, you'll be able to overwinter your bees and keep them alive during the winter months."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ba14a56-17fd-451a-ba09-eb4fcefb7710",
                                                "sense_id": "b8456554-3b9d-32df-b589-92932c191111",
                                                "text": "We overwinter our blueberry bushes in an unheated greenhouse, but when re-tubbed this year they will be too big to move. What are their chances of surviving winter outside?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b76b3ebf-bfeb-3bfc-977f-3fed94265928",
                                        "entry_id": "532925c8-2312-33b1-a0c6-790ce9ea8fa0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To spend the winter (in a particular place)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26664976-e497-448c-baf3-828e3c7fbf08",
                                                "sense_id": "b76b3ebf-bfeb-3bfc-977f-3fed94265928",
                                                "text": "Insects may overwinter in fallen fruit if it is not removed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "206edbfb-99eb-42db-a28c-c32b27eed36a",
                                                "sense_id": "b76b3ebf-bfeb-3bfc-977f-3fed94265928",
                                                "text": "Fish only overwinter in streams having a sufficient source of groundwater."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e163fbd-4bee-444c-b6e4-e80afe28e28d",
                                                "sense_id": "b76b3ebf-bfeb-3bfc-977f-3fed94265928",
                                                "text": "Different insects also differ in the way in which they overwinter. Most insects overwinter as eggs or pupae, but others overwinter as larvae or nymphs, whilst quite a few hibernate in the adult phase."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82859769-353b-4dbb-906d-5a1ebd777a33",
                                                "sense_id": "b76b3ebf-bfeb-3bfc-977f-3fed94265928",
                                                "text": "'Early Purple Sprouting' broccoli is so hardy you can let it overwinter and it rewards you with—yes, you guessed it—early purple sprouts that are tender and delicious."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "overwinter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f432073e-9869-3c03-86ac-49ad887611e8",
                                        "entry_id": "f144dc73-379d-3aa8-a935-6edefa64da18",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Occurring over the winter season."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db8d5363-b479-4467-b162-a6b84465b679",
                                                "sense_id": "f432073e-9869-3c03-86ac-49ad887611e8",
                                                "text": "The effect of seedling size on overwinter injury was analyzed separately by analysis of covariance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "521ec310-f127-4aa7-900a-dcab2ea98cbe",
                                                "sense_id": "f432073e-9869-3c03-86ac-49ad887611e8",
                                                "text": "Overwinter survival ranged from 0% to 100% and increased with increasing fall total length and winter temperatures among all cohorts and reservoirs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eddb58b6-a0b7-48d7-b318-c3ce17f69048",
                                                "sense_id": "f432073e-9869-3c03-86ac-49ad887611e8",
                                                "text": "A replicated site comparison study on 1, 031 agricultural sites across England in 2004–2008 (29) found that in three out of four year-on-year comparisons, grey partridge Perdix perdix density changes and overwinter survival were higher on sites under agri-environment schemes, than on sites not under schemes (density changes were more positive on agri-environment scheme sites than non-agi-environment scheme sites in all comparisons except 2007-2008; overwinter survival was higher for all except 2006-2007)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "overwinter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "992f02ba-d391-37a1-9cfe-39a330438c6c",
                                        "entry_id": "cf43052b-645b-3555-9dcb-4f2ce0ff3045",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "During the winter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "704aa88d-845d-4500-94f5-841d4e61cf26",
                                                "sense_id": "992f02ba-d391-37a1-9cfe-39a330438c6c",
                                                "text": "Ground cover of perennial grasses declined seriously under plots covered overwinter with dead thistle plants."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01c04a72-192a-41b3-8fd6-beb21f6f130c",
                                                "sense_id": "992f02ba-d391-37a1-9cfe-39a330438c6c",
                                                "text": "Moreover, each year of continuous corn cropping the corn stover would be turned under by fall plowing in preparation for the next spring planting, leaving the land bare overwinter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "79247404-86cf-4e11-93d4-aca3b17f0f1c",
                                                "sense_id": "992f02ba-d391-37a1-9cfe-39a330438c6c",
                                                "text": "The copepod Thermocyclops oithonoides rests overwinter as copepodids in lake mud in the Mugglesee and other lakes in Europe."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "080603d7-de2b-4e56-a5a1-ea226cdf5b63",
                        "source_entry_id": "2758cacf-c589-3585-8ec7-41992c42ff62",
                        "target_lang_word": "winter",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "winter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "60807739-72b7-37ea-be37-71701d9753f8",
                                        "entry_id": "f4e6c63e-50f4-36c0-9fd4-79a958301cab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Traditionally the fourth of the four seasons, typically regarded as spanning the months of December, January, and February in temperate and polar regions of the Northern Hemisphere or the months of June, July, and August in the Southern Hemisphere. It is the time when the sun is lowest in the sky, resulting in short days, and the time of year with the lowest atmospheric temperatures for the region."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "775f1073-2137-4f5f-b6bf-9985e7d0a074",
                                                "sense_id": "60807739-72b7-37ea-be37-71701d9753f8",
                                                "text": "Ne take noon hede to brynge togidere þe parties of þe boon þat is to-broken or dislocate, til viij. daies ben goon in þe wyntir, & v. in þe somer; for þanne it schal make quytture, and be sikir from swellynge; & þanne brynge togidere þe brynkis eiþer þe disiuncture after þe techynge þat schal be seid in þe chapitle of algebra."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b8a4c60-e457-455b-8025-55c1eee5bc62",
                                                "sense_id": "60807739-72b7-37ea-be37-71701d9753f8",
                                                "text": "And after summer evermore succeeds\n Barren winter, with his wrathful nipping cold."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cdabdada-6bd4-4a7a-8372-54c4cdfb30f5",
                                                "sense_id": "60807739-72b7-37ea-be37-71701d9753f8",
                                                "text": "It cannot be denied it [the chameleon] is (if not the moſt of any) a very abſtemious animall, and ſuch as by reaſon of its frigidity, paucity of bloud, and latitancy in the winter (about which time the obſervations are often made) will long ſubſist without a viſible ſuſtentation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e5e7aeb-0d28-4613-9343-e99a1e0376db",
                                                "sense_id": "60807739-72b7-37ea-be37-71701d9753f8",
                                                "text": "There shall he learn, ere sixteen winters old,\nThat …"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9859f2d-c71b-498b-b653-ba87b99411c9",
                                                "sense_id": "60807739-72b7-37ea-be37-71701d9753f8",
                                                "text": "[…] a woman, tall, and strong of aspect, of some thirty winters by seeming, [...]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dc72b6a9-03a6-3bd7-9f82-268c4a1d6b25",
                                        "entry_id": "f4e6c63e-50f4-36c0-9fd4-79a958301cab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The period of decay, old age, death, or the like."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "poetic",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b5222ad-a42c-4ea8-b175-1c5895f989c9",
                                                "sense_id": "dc72b6a9-03a6-3bd7-9f82-268c4a1d6b25",
                                                "text": "Life's autumn past, I stand on winter's verge."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8bbe35a-19e8-439e-9307-35ecf5749327",
                                                "sense_id": "dc72b6a9-03a6-3bd7-9f82-268c4a1d6b25",
                                                "text": "Buterin seemed to sense that the market was out of balance, and he made a smart decision that helped Ethereum weather the crypto winter and continue to build while the market was down."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0faafd94-e551-3ebd-886d-7e23116ea994",
                                        "entry_id": "f4e6c63e-50f4-36c0-9fd4-79a958301cab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone with dark skin, eyes and hair, seen as best suited to certain colors of clothing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e1924ecd-185f-3acc-ac92-77aee7f091cc",
                                        "entry_id": "f4e6c63e-50f4-36c0-9fd4-79a958301cab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An appliance to be fixed on the front of a grate, to keep a kettle warm, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "42045cae-47b9-3f6a-b126-e25b85c57602",
                                        "entry_id": "f4e6c63e-50f4-36c0-9fd4-79a958301cab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The rainy season."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "India",
                                            "archaic",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "222c6d0b-7609-409a-b560-7aea21c812a6",
                                                "sense_id": "42045cae-47b9-3f6a-b126-e25b85c57602",
                                                "text": "Note that the Citie of Goa is the principall place of all the Oriental India, and the winter thus beginneth the 15 of May, with very great raine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a5be8ee-0628-4a08-bd13-c6c8caad9576",
                                                "sense_id": "42045cae-47b9-3f6a-b126-e25b85c57602",
                                                "text": "The Winter heere beginneth about the first of Iune and dureth till the twentieth of September, but not with continuall raines as at Goa, but for some sixe or seuen dayes every change and full, with much wind, thunder and raine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75a723aa-2048-4f8e-be37-dfe912c3ab6c",
                                                "sense_id": "42045cae-47b9-3f6a-b126-e25b85c57602",
                                                "text": "In Winter (when they rarely stir) they have a Mumjama, or Wax Cloth to throw over it […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f6b08e5-f251-43e3-bb38-fb64dc2a11b9",
                                                "sense_id": "42045cae-47b9-3f6a-b126-e25b85c57602",
                                                "text": "The mere breadth of these mountains divides summer from winter, that is to say, the season of fine weather from the rainy […] all that is meant by winter in India is the time of the year when the clouds […] are driven violently by the winds against the mountains, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "winter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7751acb3-e410-3057-b6e4-7345d45fc2bd",
                                        "entry_id": "74f714a1-54ad-3552-a3f6-3d503be4271e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To spend the winter (in a particular place)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86d6ce0f-e93b-4cc0-952c-246bb8ceaae2",
                                                "sense_id": "7751acb3-e410-3057-b6e4-7345d45fc2bd",
                                                "text": "When they retired, they hoped to winter in Florida."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70d58267-edb9-441b-a438-64b88c16f0a0",
                                                "sense_id": "7751acb3-e410-3057-b6e4-7345d45fc2bd",
                                                "text": "Those who seek to invade another country anywhere across the great Eurasian steppes are condemned eventually to winter in it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e3d617fd-336a-39b1-8e63-2d0bd4faa40a",
                                        "entry_id": "74f714a1-54ad-3552-a3f6-3d503be4271e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To store something (for instance animals) somewhere over winter to protect it from cold."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
